Open a terminal and create a new LEX file, e.g., lexical.l. 
In the definitions section, include headers and declare the symbol table. 
In the rules section, define patterns for identifiers, constants, comments, and operators. 
Use { printf(...) } actions to print the recognized tokens. 
Write a helper function to insert identifiers into the symbol table. 
Save and compile the file using: 
lex lexical.l 
gcc lex.yy.c -o lexical 
Run the executable: 
./lexical < input.c> 
Observe the output and verify the tokens and symbol table entries. 
